sentences.t:
Ἑρμεία, Διὸς υἱέ, διάκτορε, δῶτορ ἑάων,
ἦ ῥά κεν ἐν δεσμοῖς ἐθέλοις κρατεροῖσι πιεσθεὶς
εὕδειν ἐν λέκτροισι παρὰ χρυσέῃ Ἀφροδίτῃ;

sentences.tr:
Hermeia, Dios huie, diaktore, dōtor heaōn,
ē rha ken en desmois ethelois krateroisi piestheis
heudein en lektroisi para chryseēi Aphroditēi;

sentences.l:
let bonds three times as many, boundless, hold me on both sides,
and you look on, gods and all goddesses,
but let me sleep beside golden Aphrodite.”

But when they had made trial with the ball straight up,
the two danced then on the much-nourishing earth,
thick and fast exchanging;

“Alcinous, lord, most conspicuous of all the people,
both you boasted that your dancers were the best,
and so indeed the matter has been made real;
